Description: EN/RU keyboard layout correction utility for Linux desktops
 OpenSwitcher is a Linux desktop utility for EN/RU typing workflows.
 It provides automatic correction of words typed in the wrong keyboard layout,
 manual correction hotkeys, selected-text layout conversion, tray integration,
 and a settings UI. The application runs as a user daemon with tray/settings
 frontends and integrates with systemd user services.
